sam: quick heads-up. a customer hit flaky gateway behavior where 502s from an upstream LB come back with body `{ "error": "bad_gateway" }` but our node SDK treats anything >=500 as a generic ApiError. they lose the ability to do typed retry logic.

lina: ouch. is this the same class of problem as rate-limit mapping? we already special-case 429.

sam: related but different: gateway transforms (502/504) vs rate-limit. customers expect a TransientError they can catch and run exponential backoff+jitter. for node folks we should expose a discriminated union error type so TS users get good narrowing.

omar: agree. proposal: introduce exported classes/errors: `RedwoodError` (base), `AuthError` (401/403), `RateLimitError` (429, includes retryAfter:number|undefined), `TransientError` (502/503/504 + originalStatus + upstream?:string), `APIError` (everything else) . keep ApiError for backward compat but Recommended usage is instance checks or `error.type` string.

kevin: how to do this without breaking too many apps? current node lib often returns an Error with httpStatus and raw body. we can subclass Error and keep old props. That should be additive. Also add `isTransient()` helper on client.

lina: can we make TS declaration file declare a discriminated union? e.g., `type RedwoodError = RateLimitError | TransientError | AuthError | APIError` and each has `kind: 'rate_limit'|'transient'|...` so `if (err.kind === 'transient') {}` is type-narrowing.

sam: yes. example usage in sample app docs:

sam: ```ts
try {
  await client.generate(req)
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof redwood.RateLimitError || err.kind === 'rate_limit') {
    const wait = err.retryAfter ?? backoff.getNext()
    await sleep(wait * 1000)
    // retry
  } else if (err.kind === 'transient') {
    // exponential jittered retry
  } else {
    throw err
  }
}
```

omar: also add `err.meta?.originalStatus` and `err.meta?.upstream` to help pinpoint gateway vs origin. we'll populate `upstream` when we parse a structured body like `{source: 'kong', ...}` if available.

kevin: tests: unit tests for headers/body parsing and an e2e that simulates a proxy returning 502 with a rate-limit-like body so we don't misclassify. add telemetry event `sdk.node.error_classified` with fields `kind` and `mapped_from_status` so we can detect mapping drift.

lina: docs: update quickstart + retries page; add snippet showing `kind` discrimination. Also add migration note for existing code that `err.status` remains available and `instanceof Error` still works.

sam: concern: some users rely on string matching of message. we should keep human-friendly `message` unchanged and encourage `kind` checks. add deprecation warning in changelog about relying on message contents.

ci-bot: ci: node-sdk/err-union -> tests passed (ci #8801) :white_check_mark:

omar: sounds good. can someone pick up the TS types + sample update? I can do the runtime classification + telemetry.

lina: i'll do TS types and docs; will sync with product on the wording for migration note.

sam: I'll open the PR for runtime error classes and a short CHANGELOG entry. linking it here once draft is up.

kevin: nice work. this will make onboarding sample apps much clearer for node users.

sam: thanks all, closing thread when PR merged.
